7. COUNCIL REVENUE INTELLIGENCE

Develop a sophisticated AI-powered council revenue analysis system.

OneGov must help councils understand WHICH AREAS ARE NOT GENERATING EXPECTED REVENUE AND WHY.

This should be one of the platform’s most impressive features.

Build an interactive GIS map showing:

* Provinces.
* Districts.
* Councils.
* Wards.
* Markets.
* Trading zones.
* Property revenue zones.
* Other configured revenue areas.

Each area should have revenue performance indicators.

For example:

Ward A:
Expected revenue: K100,000.
Actual verified revenue: K35,000.
Collection performance: 35%.

Ward B:
Expected revenue: K100,000.
Actual verified revenue: K92,000.
Collection performance: 92%.

These figures are illustrative demo data.

The AI should analyse verified available information and help explain why an area is underperforming.

Possible investigative indicators include:

* Low business registration coverage.
* Unpaid trading permits.
* Outstanding market levies.
* Unpaid property rates.
* Inactive registered businesses.
* Incomplete billing records.
* Failed or incomplete payment reconciliation.
* Collection-system downtime.
* Inconsistent records.
* Unverified revenue assessments.

Do not present assumptions as established facts.

The AI must distinguish between:

1. Confirmed findings.
2. Possible explanations.
3. Areas requiring further investigation.

Provide:

* Revenue heatmaps.
* Area comparisons.
* Revenue trend analysis.
* Collection efficiency charts.
* AI-generated investigation recommendations.
* Reports for council officers.
* Follow-up task assignments.
* Investigation status tracking.

Council officers should be able to investigate and update cases.

The system must help councils make better revenue decisions, not simply display numbers.

