12. APPLICATION WORKFLOW

Create a reusable application workflow engine.

A typical workflow:

1. User selects a government service.
2. Platform displays requirements.
3. AI assists the user in completing the application.
4. User uploads required documents.
5. Platform checks completeness.
6. Application is submitted.
7. Application is routed to the correct institution.
8. Authorised officer reviews it.
9. Officer requests additional information, approves or rejects it.
10. User receives a notification.
11. User completes any required payment.
12. Official confirmation or document is issued through the authorised institution.
13. OneGov stores the transaction record and application history.

Include configurable workflows because different institutions have different approval procedures.

